  "workflows": {},
  "implementation_policy": "A 2.09 kg polished steel ball (radius 4 cm) is released from rest 38 cm above the centre of a black rubber membrane (clear diameter 76 cm, 0.8 mm thick, E = 1.2 MPa, Poisson 0.48, pretension 65 N/m) clamped between two rings. physics/simulate_native.py solves the coupled rigid-ball / nonlinear thin-shell problem with libuipc (affine rigid body, Neo-Hookean shell, discrete-shell bending, IPC contact with friction) at dt = 1/1920 s and stores the native states (simulation.npz). Edits change one declared input through edit_vocab.py (ball mass x2, membrane modulus x0.5 / x3, delete the membrane, add an identical second ball on the drop line). appearance/render_native.py replays a native cache in the modelled laboratory workcell (Blender 4.3.2 Cycles); the published videos are the accepted saved scene of each case with the laboratory look of appearance/realism_overlay.py, which changes shaders, lights and colour only and checks geometry, animation and camera byte for byte before rendering. --stage verify checks the accepted delivery (renders/steel_ball_tensioned_membrane). Material values are nominal, not calibrated.",
